    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
What a WuWa character&apos;s own textures look like, so a mod&apos;s files can be sorted into ROLES
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Every field here describes the SOURCE -- the character whose mod is being read -- and none of
them says anything about the target, the plan or the fix. That is why this is a thing of its
own rather than part of :cpp:struct:`WWMIFixerConfig`: sorting a mod&apos;s files into roles is
CLASSIFICATION, which is the parser&apos;s job, and the fixer only needs the answer
</verbatim> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
